# ─── Do NOT set an API base URL ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is deliberately no VITE_API_URL here any more.
#
# The app always calls /api on its OWN origin, and each host proxies that to
# the backend (netlify.toml, vercel.json, vite.config.ts). Pointing the
# frontend at the Render origin directly BREAKS LOGIN/SESSIONS: the session
# cookie is SameSite=lax, which browsers refuse to send on cross-site fetch
# requests, so every call gets a brand-new empty session. The visible symptom
# is an upload reporting "Ready · N segments" while the library stays on
# "No videos yet".
#
# If a VITE_API_URL variable is still configured in your Netlify/Vercel
# dashboard, DELETE it — the code ignores it, but leaving it is misleading.

# Optional: max upload size shown in UI
VITE_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=100
